meta {
  name: 15 Try to accept an assignment that doesn't exist
  type: http
  seq: 15
}

post {
  url: {{host}}/api/agent-listings/999999/accept
  auth: bearer
  body: none
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{jwt}}
}

assert {
  res.status: gte 400
  res.status: lt 500
}

docs {
  Defensive probe. If a sneaky agent guessed an ID, can they accept it?
  Persona doc: "Cannot accept an assignment for someone else's user ID
  (403)" — but here the assignment ID doesn't even exist.

  Expected: 404 (or 403 if the service decides not to leak existence).
  Either is fine. Want to make sure error body has a clear `detail`.
}
